  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 214 AM EST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nHeights will be on the rise and warm advection will commence today \ninto tonight as a well defined upper low exits east through the\neastern Great Lakes and New England. Lake clouds will linger \nfor much of the day in lingering nw flow, though partial \nafternoon clearing and WAA could allow temps to recover into the\nlow-mid 50s.\n\nSeveral northern stream shortwaves and associated mid-upper level \njet streaks bypass north-northeast of the area Sunday through \nTuesday allowing for dry conditions, a gradual warming trend, and \nsomewhat breezy conditions at times. \n\nEnsemble guidance continues to come into better agreement in a \ndeeper negative height anomaly emerging over the eastern CONUS by \nthe second half of next week. This likely draws a cold front through \nthe area around Wednesday with another shot of cooler/breezy wx \nThursday through Saturday. Chances for measurable rain appear on the \nlow side however with flow trajectories favoring far NW IN and ne IL \naround Thu-Fri for higher lake effect rain chances.",
